  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 103.72 Public docking structure",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 103.72 “Public docking structure” means a docking structure that is owned by a political subdivision or a state or federal agency and is available for use by the general public. The term includes docking structures that are allowed to be used only by residents of the governmental unit that owns the structure as well as docking structures that are allowed to be used by any individual or group, with or without compensation or other consideration to the owner.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes #1, #2, #3, and #4 at Chapter heading for Env-Wt 100) #12801, eff 12-15-19; renumbered by #13945 (formerly Env-Wt 103.70)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt100.html"
